      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1537",
      "html": "<ul><li><strong>Scientific name:</strong> Pseudomystus stenogrammus Ng &amp; Siebert, 2005</li><li><strong>Common name:</strong> Clown Catfish</li><li><strong>Type locality:</strong> Sungai Laung at Dessa Maruwei, Sungai, Kalimantan Tengah, Borneo.</li><li><strong>Pronunciation:</strong> SUE doh MIST uss - sten oh grah muss</li><li><strong>Etymology:</strong> From the Greek pseudos, meaning lie, and mystus, a genus of bagrid catfishes. In reference to the overall similarity of the two genera.</li><li><strong>IUCN Red List:</strong> Data Deficient (last assessed 2019).</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1537",
      "html": "<p>Asia: southern Borneo, Indonesia. Pacific, Greater Sunda Island Rivers, Borneo Waters, Southern Borneo Waters.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1537",
      "html": "<p>Breeding: Unreported. There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1537",
      "html": "<p>Members of the bagrid genus Pseudomystus are small- to mid-sized freshwater catfish endemic to Southeast Asia. Pseudomystus are commonly found in swamps and rivers throughout Southeast Asia. They can be differentiated from Leiocassis by a relatively short snout and a subterminal mouth. Many Pseudomystus have a color pattern of contrasting vertical bars or blotches.</p>"
    },
